A TRUNCATED facet response for the sections facet, using the "facet_type" spelling of the name member.

ASSEMBLED to the documented facet shape; see facet-authorities.source for the structure and the vendor
citations. This fixture is deliberately internally inconsistent in one specific way, and that
inconsistency is the whole point: facets[].count is 10842 while details carries 2 entries.

Two things it pins, both of which are real risks rather than hypotheticals.

1. TRUNCATION MUST BE VISIBLE.
   https://developerdocs.instructure.com/services/ab-connect/introduction/facets.md states "AB Connect
   does not support paging of facet data" and "When requesting facets with a large number of values
   (count > 10,000) only the first 10,000 entries are returned". 01-sdk-v3.md section 6.3 forbids
   GetFacetAsync from attempting a second call, so the only honest response is to report the shortfall.
   A test must assert ABFacet.IsTruncated is TRUE here and ReportedCount is 10842, because
   ReportedCount > Values.Count. A projection that returned only the values, or that overwrote
   ReportedCount with Values.Count, would make a truncated facet indistinguishable from a complete one,
   and a consumer would enumerate 10,000 sections out of 10,842 and believe it had them all.
   The real detail count is shortened to 2 here rather than padded to 10,000 so the file stays readable;
   only the relationship ReportedCount > Values.Count is load-bearing, not the specific sizes.

2. THE NAME MEMBER HAS TWO SPELLINGS.
   This is the only fixture that uses "facet_type" instead of "facet". The payloads this SDK's
   predecessor consumed in production carried "facet", while the AB Connect documentation and
   01-sdk-v3.md both refer to the member as the facet_type discriminator. ABFacetBlock accepts either
   and reads whichever is present, because one of the two spellings being wrong must not silently
   produce an empty facet. A test must read ABFacetNames.Sections off this fixture and off
   facet-authorities.json's "facet" member and get the right name from both.

Section counts and open issue 8: the count here is over 10,000 on purpose. 01-sdk-v3.md open issue 8
records that if the OnCourse license exceeds 10,000 sections then section enumeration by facet is not
viable at all and the hierarchy must be derived from standards rows instead. This fixture is what that
decision looks like arriving in code: IsTruncated true on ABFacetNames.Sections is the signal to switch
strategies, and it is why the XML documentation on ABFacetNames.Sections says to always check it.
